Subject: ui: declare the vendored symfony/yaml as the pinned release

Zabbix vendors symfony/yaml v5.1.3 in ui/vendor. That release is affected by
CVE-2026-109413 (uncontrolled recursion in the YAML parser, reachable through
configuration import) and CVE-2026-45133, CVE-2026-45304 and CVE-2026-45305,
fixed in 5.4.52 and 5.4.54. The package build replaces ui/vendor/symfony/yaml
with the pinned upstream v5.4.56 tag, a 5.x release whose requirements the
vendored symfony/deprecation-contracts and symfony/polyfill-ctype satisfy.
This patch moves the Composer pin, lock entry and installed metadata to the
values Composer records for that tag, so InstalledVersions and the SBOM report
the code that ships. The lock content-hash is left as upstream ships it;
upstream's lock is already out of date with its composer.json.

Origin: DHI-internal (values from https://github.com/symfony/yaml/blob/v5.4.56/composer.json and https://repo.packagist.org/p2/symfony/yaml.json)
Base-Tree: tarball https://cdn.zabbix.com/zabbix/sources/stable/7.0/zabbix-7.0.32.tar.gz sha256:ead5b0723ad965eb0e79f98d5d2b89088e7c898ae194eeba767e5d1fb2d50a96 path=zabbix-7.0.32
Verify: cmd `go test ./package/main/zabbix-web-nginx-pgsql/tests -run TestProductDEB -count=1` expect "ok"
Forwarded: not-needed (dependency choice in ui/composer.json that upstream has not updated)
Drop-When: dependency symfony/yaml >= 5.4.54 (pinned by ui/composer.lock in the Zabbix release tarball)
CVE: CVE-2026-109413
CVE: CVE-2026-45133
CVE: CVE-2026-45304
CVE: CVE-2026-45305

